@startuml seq-restore
!include _style.iuml
title Restoring a backup while the app runs

actor User
participant "BackupsSettingsPage /\nMainPage (1.x import)" as Page
participant RestoreFlow as Flow
participant App
participant HotkeyListener
participant BrowserConnector
participant BackupScheduler
participant StorageService
participant RestoreService
database "LocalState" as Files
database "restore-work" as Work

User -> Page : select backup, parts, Restore...\n(first start: Import from TextTemplateManager 1)
Page -> Flow : RunAsync(path, parts, confirm)
Flow -> RestoreService : FindSyncLocationIssues / FindChangedSyncFiles /\nFindSyncedFolderTargets
Flow -> User : confirm (the page only);\nper missing sync file: recreate here, choose a location\n(synced folders chosen) or link another file, leave missing;\nper changed existing file (synced folders chosen):\noverwrite or keep (-> SyncFilePlacement list)
Flow -> App : RestoreFromBackupAsync(path, parts, placements)
App -> App : PersistPendingAsync()\n(saves + a recent backup of the current state)
App -> HotkeyListener : Register("None")
App -> BrowserConnector : Stop()
App -> BackupScheduler : StopAsync()
App -> StorageService : SuspendWritesAsync()\n(every later save is dropped)
App -> RestoreService : RestoreAsync(path, parts, placements)
activate RestoreService
RestoreService -> RestoreService : RecoverInterrupted(), Verify(backup)
RestoreService -> RestoreService : plan: data (all, or local / synced part mixed\nwith the current file), settings (1.x: merged over\ncurrent; 2.x: keeps tour + version state),\nsync settings (paths from placements), sync file copies;\nkept existing files: their folder's cached copy left out
RestoreService -> Work : write each new file to new/<n>, flushed
RestoreService -> Work : copy each current target to old/<n>\nwrite journal.json, flushed
RestoreService -> Files : move new/<n> over each target
alt a move failed
  RestoreService -> Files : RollBack(journal)
  RestoreService --> App : failed, nothing changed
  App -> StorageService : ResumeWrites()
  App -> App : hotkey, connector, scheduler back on
else all moved
  RestoreService -> Work : delete restore-work
  RestoreService --> App : succeeded
  deactivate RestoreService
  App -> App : tray off, instance key unregistered,\nAppInstance.Restart() -> loads the restored files
end
note over RestoreService, Files
  A crash between journal and cleanup is undone by
  RecoverInterrupted() at the next start.
end note
@enduml
